This repository presents a detailed analysis of the convergence properties of two binomial option pricing models—the Cox-Ross-Rubinstein (CRR) model and the Leisen-Reimer (LR) model—using the Black-Scholes analytical solution as a benchmark. 

The project's primary objective is to examine the speed and stability with which prices generated by the CRR and LR models converge to the Black-Scholes price, testing them under various market conditions, including different levels of moneyness (At-The-Money, In-The-Money, Out-Of-The-Money) and varying volatility regimes.
